{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277167-game-idea-you-re-not-my-high-priest","id":277167,"title":"Game Idea: \"You're Not My High Priest!\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-10T06:44:08-07:00","id":277167,"title":"Game Idea: \"You're Not My High Priest!\"","content":"Silly-sounding title, I know, but I think the idea has merit.<br /> <br /> Basically, the characters are awakened by somebody claiming to be a member of one of their cults, presumably high-ranking. They dispatch the Arisen to obtain a heavily-guarded Relic, though this is just a ruse. Secretly, the &quot;high priest&quot; wants them for &lt;some sort of ulterior motive involving the destruction of a lot of property&gt;.<br /> <br /> That's where the general premise ends. More specific would be stuff like the summoner's motives, investigating how the mummies all managed to be stolen from their cults (if they actually were), why did the summoner need &gt;1 Arisen. Was the intent to make the Arisen lose face with their guilds? Was one of the party responsible for this, and the high priest was acting on orders from a previous Descent?<br /> <br /> I'm trying to come up with a good pitch for some players who haven't done Mummy before at all. My idea is &quot;Somebody awakens you for ulterior, sinister reasons.&quot; Naturally, at first the players wouldn't know that.<br /> <br /> Basically just brainstorming. Any ideas?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T07:38:43-07:00","id":277221,"title":"","content":"If your players are ok with not starting with a Cult, you could easily have a situation in which they all once belonged to the same Cult, but were later abandoned. The false priest was just lucky enough to stumble across an entire cache of Mummies in one place. The more disparate the group, the harder it's going to be to justify all of them being in the one place for this to take place. Although if one member of the group is actually behind it all, well, that certainly provides an excuse. It's probably both the easiest explanation for this scenario, and one of the most entertaining.<br /> <br /> Rather than raising them for a bit of relic hunting, why wouldn't the false priest just raise them with the purpose he desires? Then the entire group has a Judge-enforced Purpose that they must follow, or else lose Sekhem. Bonus points if it's a historical setting (you could run this as prelude to a modern campaign, if you want). If you set it in a time/place of turmoil, like modern Iraq/Syria, China in pretty much the entire first half of the 20th century, the French Revolution, or something similar, it's pretty easy to justify both multiple mummies and thoroughly human motivations for violent purposes. I remember an idea floating around somewhere about a Nazi occultist raising a Mummy to help defend Germany, to name one suggestion following a similar theme to your ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T08:14:44-07:00","id":277232,"title":"","content":"Well, presumably, our Sinister Summoner fears retribution from the Arisen if they discover what his intentions were after the fact. Once you're finished with your Task, you immediately lose a Sekhem and are free to do whatever you want for the rest of your Descent, correct?* I remember reading an Actual Play where after the Arisen destroyed a drug den for his summoner, he turned around and burned the summoner away for wasting his time.<br /> <br /> And if the true goal was by one of the party members seeking something heretical, it definitely doesn't want the rest of the meret to catch wind of it, I'd imagine.<br /> <br /> But that's just reasoning for why a Sinister Summoner would want to keep their motives secret.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of a legit high priest being coerced into summoning the mummies to help some sort of historical villain group, like the Nazis. Honest, mixing Nazis and Mummies just strikes me as a golden adventure hook.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Pursuant to the normal Sekhem drop rules, of course.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T08:16:10-07:00","id":277233,"title":"","content":"You have two cows. One is your high priest-wait, no, that can't be right.<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling</b>: The mummy has two cows. You are totally his high priest.<br /> <br /> Sorry, had to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T08:21:41-07:00","id":277236,"title":"","content":"I feel like something magical is just flying right over my head. Can you elaborate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T08:26:33-07:00","id":277239,"title":"","content":"The changeling is the cow. The changeling is the high priest. Mummies have terrible memories. Fae are sometimes known for being mischievous.<br /> <br /> The joke is apparently an Exalted thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T09:25:40-07:00","id":277290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277167-game-idea-you-re-not-my-high-priest?p=277239#post277239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The changeling is the cow. The changeling is the high priest. Mummies have terrible memories. Fae are sometimes known for being mischievous.<br /> <br /> The joke is apparently an Exalted thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I looked up several threads of &quot;You have two cows&quot; jokes. Thank you for referring me.<br /> <br /> I also get the joke now. Have a cookie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:25:55-07:00","id":277486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277167-game-idea-you-re-not-my-high-priest?p=277232#post277232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honest, mixing Nazis and Mummies just strikes me as a golden adventure hook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering how Arisen wouldn't really understand skin-color- or ethnicity-based racism or even sexism, but would <i>totally </i>grok the notion of conquest, new world order, <i>lebensraum</i> and military organizations with occult hierarchies...I think it'd go together pretty damn well. The core of the SS was already Himmler's cult that planned to subvert Christianity in favor of a more mystical religion once the Reich finished conquering everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:26:42-07:00","id":277487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277167-game-idea-you-re-not-my-high-priest#post277167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to come up with a good pitch for some players who haven't done Mummy before at all. My idea is &quot;Somebody awakens you for ulterior, sinister reasons.&quot; Naturally, at first the players wouldn't know that.<br /> <br /> Basically just brainstorming. Any ideas?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/11948-1001-mummy-story-hooks\">A few, yes. </a>Including the one from your original post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T12:43:03-07:00","id":277503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/277167-game-idea-you-re-not-my-high-priest?p=277486#post277486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how Arisen wouldn't really understand skin-color- or ethnicity-based racism or even sexism, but would <i>totally </i>grok the notion of conquest, new world order, <i>lebensraum</i> and military organizations with occult hierarchies...I think it'd go together pretty damn well. The core of the SS was already Himmler's cult that planned to subvert Christianity in favor of a more mystical religion once the Reich finished conquering everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, one of the guilds(the Maa-Kep, I think) think Hitler's only sin was to <i>lose</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T13:34:34-07:00","id":277526,"title":"","content":"Yeah, though I'm sure certain members of the Maa-Kep would disagree: those with predominantly Jewish or non-Aryan Cults, or in areas badly ravaged by the war.<br /> <br /> That's the funny thing to me, the Maa-Kep are easily my favorite Guild, but their views on some issues <i>really </i>squick me out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T19:05:16-07:00","id":277751,"title":"","content":"Heh, I actually had a sinister summoner storyline. In this case, the high priest was the legit heirophant of the main mummy NPC. However, said priest resented the arisen and the hard life hes had to lead, so hes decided to turn the arisen on each other in hopes to destroy them all. To that end, he has his own Cult that has infiltrated the cults of the Nomarchs and has been directing the cults against each other. To add a little personal torture to his successor, he summoned his Mummy lover and commanded the mummy to kill him. Sekhem driven by Purpose, things got messed up pretty quickly (imagine five nights at freddies, but with a mummy and brainwashed cultists).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}